{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "A Day With Vanessa", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Last Minute Cancellation", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 4, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 16, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Use expressions about relationships and feelings in a range of social and work contexts. ", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Pronouncing the Suffix -tion", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Suffixes are parts of words that are at the end. They often indicate the form of the word.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " One of the most common suffixes is <span class=\"italic\">-tion</span>. This indicates that the word is a noun.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": " To reserve - Reserva<span class=\"strong\">tion</span><br/>To compete - Competi<span class=\"strong\">tion</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " The suffix <span class=\"italic\">-tion</span> is pronounced with a /sh/ sound and a schwa. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": " You stress the syllable that comes right before the suffix.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Say these words. Stress the bolded syllable.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<br/>reser<span class=\"strong\">va</span>tion<br/>compe<span class=\"strong\">ti</span>tion<br/>re<span class=\"strong\">a</span>ction<br/>cancel<span class=\"strong\">la</span>tion<br/>att<span class=\"strong\">en</span>tion<br/>introd<span class=\"strong\">uc</span>tion<br/>sani<span class=\"strong\">ta</span>tion<br/><span class=\"strong\">op</span>tion", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I made reservations at the restaurant next to the art gallery. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'm a little worried about my bistro - there's so much more competition!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Look, there's a new exhibition coming next month! ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Stressing New Information", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "In conversation, it is not always WHAT you say but HOW you say it. You can use stress to introduce new information and to show that you are listening and understand other people's feelings.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Usually, the stressed words in a sentence are the nouns, verbs, adjectives and adverbs. <br/>Sometimes, you can choose to stress other types of words to show that you are adding new information or showing that you understand other people's feelings.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I'm famished after all that walking! I feel like a bowl of pasta!<br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: A <span class=\"strong\">giant</span> bowl of pasta! I'm starving, too! </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In this case, Sally stresses <span class=\"strong\">giant</span>. She is adding new information to the idea of a bowl of pasta and she is showing that she understands Vanessa's feeling of being hungry.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can stress words like <span class=\"italic\">really</span> when you want to show empathy. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">That's got to be <span class=\"strong\">really</span> worrying!</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Look, there's a new exhibition coming next month! We have to go!<br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: <span class=\"underline\">Which</span> exhibition? ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "famished", "type": "name"}, {"content": "very hungry", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I'm famished after all that walking! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le16ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about social activities.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to pop up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to suddenly appear", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There are more restaurants popping up in this neighborhood lately.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le16ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "last time I checked", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to talk about the last time you looked at something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Last time I checked, there were at least twenty. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le16ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to lose track of time", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to not notice the passing of time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Oh no! The reservation was for 1:00. I lost track of time!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le16ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sculptor", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who makes a sculpture", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He is a famous sculptor.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le16ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn7le16ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "On the Internet, go to YouTube and find the song \"T-I-O-N Electric Company\".", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Listen to the song and write down all the words you hear that end with the -tion sound.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Watch the video to see if you got all the words! Check your spelling.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Repeat the words aloud.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I pronounce words with the sound <span class=\"italic\">-tion</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I show I understand someone's feelings or situation by stressing new information.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I link words with the same consonant sound.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn7le16ob04re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn7le16ob04re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn7le16ob04re2img05.jpg", "text": "", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"image": "engenn7le16ob04re2img05.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:     I'm famished after all that walking! I feel like a bowl of pasta!<br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:         A giant bowl of pasta! I'm starving, too! I made reservations at the restaurant next to the art gallery. <br/><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:     That's that Italian place, right? There are more restaurants popping up in this neighborhood lately. I'm a little worried about my bistro - there's so much more competition!", "time": "100", "id": 1}, {"image": "engenn7le16ob04re2img01.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:         How many new restaurants are there, do you know?<br/><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:     Last time I checked, there were at least twenty. <br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:         Twenty! That's got to be really worrying! <br/><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:     Your reaction is stronger than mine and I'm the one who has a restaurant!", "time": "22000", "id": 2}, {"image": "engenn7le16ob04re2img05.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:          What time is it?<br/><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:     It's 1:30. <br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:         Really? Oh no! The reservation was for 1:00. I lost track of time!<br/><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:     Do you have the phone number? We can call and cancel.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:         Let's just walk over. There's a path through the museum.", "time": "37000", "id": 3}, {"image": "engenn7le16ob04re2img01.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:     Ooh! Look, there's a new exhibition coming next month! We have to go!<br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:         Which exhibition? <br/><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:     The Matthew Barney one. He does art installations as well. He is a famous sculptor.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:         Ah, here's the restaurant. I'll go in and make sure the reservation is canceled. I feel like going somewhere else anyway.", "time": "53000", "id": 4}]}}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can say and use the sound <span class=\"italic\">-tion</span>.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can show I understand someone's feelings or situation.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can link words with the same consonant sound.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " When you're really hungry, what do you like to eat? Why?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What gets you worried? Why?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Pronunciation Spot: A giant bowl of pasta! I'm starving, too!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "img_path": "", "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " Sally and Vanessa are hungry. Who <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">feels like</span> a bowl of pasta?", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Who